  "description": "Conformance test 33d (ZQ4): the draft queries. The harness clears the real-mode flag directly, as HighlightParcels does (the fourth / sixth call argument). No real networks. The street stub has a draft at (5, 5) with mask {1, 0, 1, 0} (edges −x, −z, +x, +z), the dirt-road stub one at (6, 6) with {0, 1, 0, 1}; both log their OccupantExists calls. ExistsNetworkOfType (§8.8): (5, 5, 0x808) true and (6, 6, 0x808) false [quirk: with bit 3 set only the street stub is asked]; (6, 6, 0x800) true from the dirt-road stub; (5, 5, 0x1F4F) true, (6, 6, 0x1F4F) false; (5, 5, 0x1) false with no stub call. ExistsConnectionOfType (§7.13): (5, 5, 0x8, s, 3) for s = 0..3 false, true, false, true (edges 1, 2, 3, 0); (6, 6, 0x8, 0, 3) true (the street stub says no, the dirt-road stub is asked with 0x800, byte 1); (5, 5, 0x800, 1, 0) true (the street stub first, the type ignored); (6, 6, 0x808, −1, 11) true [quirk: e = −1 reads byte 3], side 4 the same; (5, 5, 0x808, −1, 3) false (byte 3 = 0); (5, 5, 0x1, 1, 0) false with no stub call. In real mode every query is false and no stub is called.",
  "steps": [
